id: pm-web-crdr
title: Certify pm-web complete tracker reads and refresh the package catalog
description: "Replace every internal whole-workspace list-all consumer with one canonical strict full doubly-unbounded list --all reader certified by the public pm SDK, while preserving intentionally paginated HTTP list routes; update the runtime/tooling pins and synchronize the install catalog with the exact manifests of every fleet extension."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-21T11:07:28.820Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T11:45:56.110Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-21T11:41:29.112Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-21T11:41:29.112Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "One shared reader owns every whole-workspace corpus load; the exact canonical argv and SDK certificate failure modes are covered; graph, board, search, calendar, export and other whole-corpus consumers fail closed rather than silently accepting omissions; client-facing paginated list endpoints preserve cursor semantics; the catalog exactly mirrors all fleet manifests including pm-rl; runtime/tooling use pm CLI 2026.8.21 and pm-changelog/pm-ops 2026.8.17; Node floor is exact in CI/release; real PostgreSQL integration, SDK, installed CLI, npm and Bun acceptance are green; independent exact-coverage and reachable-history privacy blockers remain explicit"
definition_of_ready: "Main is clean at 77a0377; the real PostgreSQL release gate reproduces one stale pm-rl catalog failure; package coverage is 64.49 lines, 81.41 branches and 58.07 functions; internal list-all calls omit completeness proof; npm reports newer pm CLI, pm-changelog and pm-ops versions."
reviewer: greptile
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-08-canonical-readers
release: next
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: "pm-web 2026.8.17, exact runtime pm CLI/SDK 2026.8.21, Node 22.19.0, real PostgreSQL on 127.0.0.1:55433, fresh npm and Bun projects"
repro_steps: "Run npm run release:check with the real test database: catalog parity fails because pm-rl changed; inspect src/routes/pm.ts and observe whole-corpus list-all calls without strict-read, no-truncate, full projection, or both unbounded output controls."
resolution: "Centralized all whole-workspace reads behind SDK certification and verified supplemental receipts, preserved paginated compatibility routes, refreshed the full fleet catalog and current dependencies, pinned workflow supply-chain inputs, added fresh packed npm and Bun acceptance, and removed duplicate command JSON through the public SDK output protocol."
expected_result: "Every full-project view is derived only from a verified complete corpus and the UI offers an accurate, current catalog for every pm package."
actual_result: "The real PostgreSQL gate passes 289 tests with 66.18 percent lines, 80.40 percent branches, and 60.45 percent functions across 26 configured sources and thresholds ratcheted to 66/80/60. All 528 declarations across 78 TypeScript files are documented. Fresh packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx scenarios activate the extension on pm 2026.8.21 and return one parseable status payload without deprecated diagnostics. Production audit is zero and npm pack contains 232 published files. Exact all-source coverage items pm-web-9ulj and pm-web-ulgy plus privacy item pm-web-priv and GitHub issue 96 remain open, so the branch must not merge or publish."
affected_version: pm-web 2026.8.17
component: routes/pm.ts complete-corpus reads and package catalog
customer_impact: "A silently partial corpus can hide work from graph, board, search, calendar and export views, while stale catalog metadata misrepresents installable package functionality."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
